WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:07.605
To subtract bigger numbers, we work one place at a time. Let's find fifty-two minus twenty-seven.

00:08.055 --> 00:14.116
Start with the ones. Two minus seven? We can't take seven away from two.

00:14.566 --> 00:20.547
So we regroup. We borrow one ten from the five tens. Now there are four tens,

00:20.547 --> 00:23.343
and the two ones become twelve ones.

00:23.793 --> 00:28.530
Now we can subtract the ones. Twelve minus seven is five.

00:28.980 --> 00:33.159
Then the tens. Four tens minus two tens is two tens.

00:33.609 --> 00:39.654
Put the parts together. Twenty plus five makes twenty-five. Check it by adding.

00:39.654 --> 00:42.944
Twenty-five plus twenty-seven is fifty-two.
